P16 PARITY AUDIT — inflate.lua → inflate.c location map
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
createBitStream / readBits         lua 5-38 → BitStream bs_read_bits
  (LSB-first bit buffer)               (-1 == Lua nil at EOF); alignByte.
buildHuffmanTable                  lua 41-81 → canonical next_code walk,
                                     per-symbol bit reversal for LSB-first,
                                     entries sorted by len. C tie-break by
                                     symbol is deterministic; Lua's unstable
                                     sort is order-irrelevant (codes within
                                     a length are unique).
decodeSymbol                       lua 83-98 → incremental LSB-first
                                     accumulation vs reversed codes.
getFixedTables                     lua 103-116 → cached statics, lit
                                     8x144/9x112/7x24/8x8, dist 5x32.
lengthBase/Extra distBase/Extra    lua 118-142 → identical tables.
clOrder                            lua 144 → identical.
Inflate.decompress                 lua 146-267 → one-shot inflate:
  zlib CMF/FLG detect+skip             ((cmf&0xF)==8 && %31==0), +4 if
  preset-dict flag; btype 0 alignByte  LEN/NLEN byte loop; btype 1 fixed;
  btype 2 dynamic (hlit/hdist/hclen, repeat syms 16/17/18); symbol loop
  with Tasks.yieldCheck() at the same positions; match copies emit 0 for
  pre-output sources (`or 0` quirk); truncated input returns partial.
  QUIRK: btype==3 falls through silently (loop re-reads headers).
Inflate.createStream               lua 278-427 → streaming reader:
  pending queue + sliding window       trimmed past 64KB keeping the most
  recent half (steady-state 32769 entries, same content as Lua's
  unpack(win,32769) trim); modes block/uncompressed/huff; read(n) returns
  up to n bytes, 0 == nil at end. Stream path guards btype==3 as EOF to
  avoid an infinite pump (one-shot keeps the faithful fall-through).

